<title>SINGAPORE: Parkway unit to launch Indonesian IPO.</title>
<headline>Parkway unit to launch Indonesian IPO.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Parkway Holdings Ltd said on Tuesday it planned to offer up to 47 million new ordinary shares in its Indonesian unit, PT Siloam Gleneagles Health Care, in an initial public offer in Indonesia.</p>
<p>It said in a statement it was offering the shares for public subscription, instead of by placement as originally planned, due to investor interest and market factors.</p>
<p>The shares would be listed on the Surabaya Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Parkway's subsidiary Gleneagles Development Pte Ltd has a 30 percent stake in Siloam.  </p>
<p>The statement said Parkway would also restructure its two hospitals and diagnostic centre in Indonesia with Siloam's existing hospital.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
